{
  "slug": "how-car-accident-determining-fault-by-location-of-damage-works",
  "title": "How Car Accident Determining Fault by Location of Damage Works",
  "excerpt": "After a collision, it doesn’t take long for blame to enter the conversation. Whether it’s two drivers on the roadside or an insurance adjuster reviewing photos, the question of who caused the crash is often at the center. One thing we’re asked all the time is: can the location of vehicle damage tell the story? […]",
  "publishedAt": "2025-09-05T10:27:12",
  "modifiedAt": "2026-04-15T14:52:49",
  "categories": [
    "auto-accident"
  ],
  "body": [
    {
      "_type": "block",
      "_key": "b75v",
      "style": "normal",
      "markDefs": [],
      "children": [
        {
          "_type": "span",
          "_key": "s75u",
          "text": "After a collision, it doesn’t take long for blame to enter the conversation. Whether it’s two drivers on the roadside or an insurance adjuster reviewing photos, the question of who caused the crash is often at the center. One thing we’re asked all the time is: can the location of vehicle damage tell the story? In many cases, yes—but not in isolation. It’s a piece of the puzzle, not the whole picture.",
          "marks": []
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "_type": "block",
      "_key": "b762",
      "style": "normal",
      "markDefs": [
        {
          "_key": "l75z",
          "_type": "link",
          "href": "/"
        }
      ],
      "children": [
        {
          "_type": "span",
          "_key": "s75w",
          "text": "Next, we will break down ",
          "marks": []
        },
        {
          "_type": "span",
          "_key": "s75x",
          "text": "how car accident determining fault by location of damage works",
          "marks": [
            "strong"
          ]
        },
        {
          "_type": "span",
          "_key": "s75y",
          "text": " in Colorado and why it matters when building a case with ",
          "marks": []
        },
        {
          "_type": "span",
          "_key": "s760",
          "text": "Dormer Harpring",
          "marks": [
            "l75z",
            "strong"
          ]
        },
        {
          "_type": "span",
          "_key": "s761",
          "text": " by your side.",
          "marks": []
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "_type": "image",
      "_key": "i763",
      "src": "./images/2025-09-shutterstock_2557451235-1.jpg",
      "alt": "Car Crash"
    },
    {
      "_type": "block",
      "_key": "b765",
      "style": "h2",
      "markDefs": [],
      "children": [
        {
          "_type": "span",
          "_key": "s764",
          "text": "Importance of Determining Fault in a Car Accident",
          "marks": [
            "strong"
          ]
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "_type": "block",
      "_key": "b767",
      "style": "normal",
      "markDefs": [],
      "children": [
        {
          "_type": "span",
          "_key": "s766",
          "text": "Assigning fault plays a central role in personal injury claims and insurance payouts. In Colorado, the party found liable for the crash is also responsible for damages, including medical expenses, lost income, and property repair. Injured drivers risk having their claims undervalued or denied altogether without a clear understanding of how fault is determined.",
          "marks": []
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "_type": "block",
      "_key": "b769",
      "style": "normal",
      "markDefs": [],
      "children": [
        {
          "_type": "span",
          "_key": "s768",
          "text": "Fault determination also affects whether you’re eligible for compensation at all. If you’re found to be primarily responsible for a collision, you could be barred from recovering any damages. That’s why we work closely with our clients from day one to gather substantial evidence, including vehicle damage photos and crash scene details.",
          "marks": []
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "_type": "block",
      "_key": "b76b",
      "style": "h2",
      "markDefs": [],
      "children": [
        {
          "_type": "span",
          "_key": "s76a",
          "text": "Understanding Colorado’s Comparative Negligence Law",
          "marks": [
            "strong"
          ]
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "_type": "block",
      "_key": "b76d",
      "style": "h3",
      "markDefs": [],
      "children": [
        {
          "_type": "span",
          "_key": "s76c",
          "text": "What is Comparative Negligence?",
          "marks": []
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "_type": "block",
      "_key": "b76f",
      "style": "normal",
      "markDefs": [],
      "children": [
        {
          "_type": "span",
          "_key": "s76e",
          "text": "Comparative negligence is a legal concept that helps determine how fault is divided in accidents where more than one party may be to blame. Rather than assigning all responsibility to one individual, this rule allows for a shared approach to liability. It recognizes that accidents often result from a combination of missteps—for example, one driver may have been speeding while the other failed to yield.",
          "marks": []
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "_type": "block",
      "_key": "b76k",
      "style": "normal",
      "markDefs": [
        {
          "_key": "l76h",
          "_type": "link",
          "href": "/denver-car-accident-lawyer/"
        }
      ],
      "children": [
        {
          "_type": "span",
          "_key": "s76g",
          "text": "In Colorado ",
          "marks": []
        },
        {
          "_type": "span",
          "_key": "s76i",
          "text": "car accident cases,",
          "marks": [
            "l76h"
          ]
        },
        {
          "_type": "span",
          "_key": "s76j",
          "text": " comparative negligence is key in deciding how much compensation each party may receive or owe. Even if you contributed to the crash somehow, you may still have a right to recover damages, as long as your share of the blame stays below the legal limit.",
          "marks": []
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "_type": "block",
      "_key": "b76m",
      "style": "h3",
      "markDefs": [],
      "children": [
        {
          "_type": "span",
          "_key": "s76l",
          "text": "Colorado’s Modified Comparative Negligence",
          "marks": []
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "_type": "block",
      "_key": "b76w",
      "style": "normal",
      "markDefs": [
        {
          "_key": "l76q",
          "_type": "link",
          "href": "https://colorado.public.law/statutes/crs_13-21-111"
        }
      ],
      "children": [
        {
          "_type": "span",
          "_key": "s76n",
          "text": "Colorado uses a ",
          "marks": []
        },
        {
          "_type": "span",
          "_key": "s76o",
          "text": "modified comparative negligence",
          "marks": [
            "strong"
          ]
        },
        {
          "_type": "span",
          "_key": "s76p",
          "text": " system, introducing a critical threshold: the 50% bar. Under",
          "marks": []
        },
        {
          "_type": "span",
          "_key": "s76r",
          "text": " Colorado Revised Statutes §13-21-111",
          "marks": [
            "l76q"
          ]
        },
        {
          "_type": "span",
          "_key": "s76t",
          "text": ", an injured person can seek compensation ",
          "marks": []
        },
        {
          "_type": "span",
          "_key": "s76u",
          "text": "only if their share of fault is less than 50%",
          "marks": [
            "strong"
          ]
        },
        {
          "_type": "span",
          "_key": "s76v",
          "text": ". They are legally barred from recovering any damages if they’re found to be 50% or more at fault.",
          "marks": []
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "_type": "block",
      "_key": "b76y",
      "style": "normal",
      "markDefs": [],
      "children": [
        {
          "_type": "span",
          "_key": "s76x",
          "text": "What does that look like in practice? Let’s say you’re awarded $100,000 in damages but are found to be 30% responsible for the crash. Your total recovery would be reduced by that same percentage, bringing your final compensation to $70,000.",
          "marks": []
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "_type": "block",
      "_key": "b770",
      "style": "normal",
      "markDefs": [],
      "children": [
        {
          "_type": "span",
          "_key": "s76z",
          "text": "This modified rule adds significant weight to the fault determination process and underscores why a strong legal strategy matters when navigating fault in a Colorado car accident case.",
          "marks": []
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "_type": "block",
      "_key": "b772",
      "style": "h2",
      "markDefs": [],
      "children": [
        {
          "_type": "span",
          "_key": "s771",
          "text": "Common Factors Used to Determine Fault",
          "marks": [
            "strong"
          ]
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "_type": "block",
      "_key": "b774",
      "style": "h3",
      "markDefs": [],
      "children": [
        {
          "_type": "span",
          "_key": "s773",
          "text": "Police Reports",
          "marks": []
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "_type": "block",
      "_key": "b776",
      "style": "normal",
      "markDefs": [],
      "children": [
        {
          "_type": "span",
          "_key": "s775",
          "text": "One of the first documents reviewed after a crash is the police report. Police officers are trained to observe vehicle positions, speak with witnesses, and document statements from involved drivers. Their findings carry significant weight with insurers and in court.",
          "marks": []
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "_type": "block",
      "_key": "b778",
      "style": "h3",
      "markDefs": [],
      "children": [
        {
          "_type": "span",
          "_key": "s777",
          "text": "Witness Testimony",
          "marks": []
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "_type": "block",
      "_key": "b77a",
      "style": "normal",
      "markDefs": [],
      "children": [
        {
          "_type": "span",
          "_key": "s779",
          "text": "Independent witnesses can provide powerful third-party perspectives, especially in cases where each driver has a different account. A reliable witness who saw one driver run a red light or fail to yield can make the difference in proving liability.",
          "marks": []
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "_type": "block",
      "_key": "b77c",
      "style": "h3",
      "markDefs": [],
      "children": [
        {
          "_type": "span",
          "_key": "s77b",
          "text": "Traffic Violations",
          "marks": []
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "_type": "block",
      "_key": "b77e",
      "style": "normal",
      "markDefs": [],
      "children": [
        {
          "_type": "span",
          "_key": "s77d",
          "text": "If one of the drivers violated a traffic law—such as speeding, texting while driving, or failing to signal—that violation can serve as strong evidence of fault. Citations issued at the scene can also strengthen a personal injury claim.",
          "marks": []
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "_type": "block",
      "_key": "b77g",
      "style": "h3",
      "markDefs": [],
      "children": [
        {
          "_type": "span",
          "_key": "s77f",
          "text": "Accident Reconstruction",
          "marks": []
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "_type": "block",
      "_key": "b77i",
      "style": "normal",
      "markDefs": [],
      "children": [
        {
          "_type": "span",
          "_key": "s77h",
          "text": "In more complex cases, we may bring in accident reconstruction specialists. These professionals analyze physical evidence like skid marks, point of impact, and vehicle trajectories to create a scientifically grounded narrative of what occurred.",
          "marks": []
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "_type": "block",
      "_key": "b77k",
      "style": "h3",
      "markDefs": [],
      "children": [
        {
          "_type": "span",
          "_key": "s77j",
          "text": "Comparative Negligence",
          "marks": []
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "_type": "block",
      "_key": "b77m",
      "style": "normal",
      "markDefs": [],
      "children": [
        {
          "_type": "span",
          "_key": "s77l",
          "text": "It’s common for multiple contributing factors to exist. For example, both drivers may have made small mistakes that led to the crash. In these cases, we work to minimize your attributed fault percentage by highlighting the other party’s more significant errors.",
          "marks": []
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "_type": "block",
      "_key": "b77o",
      "style": "h2",
      "markDefs": [],
      "children": [
        {
          "_type": "span",
          "_key": "s77n",
          "text": "The Role of Insurance Companies in Determining Fault",
          "marks": [
            "strong"
          ]
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "_type": "block",
      "_key": "b77s",
      "style": "normal",
      "markDefs": [],
      "children": [
        {
          "_type": "span",
          "_key": "s77p",
          "text": "Insurance adjusters play a significant role in the early stages of fault determination. After receiving accident reports and photos of vehicle damage, they assess statements from all parties and apply internal guidelines to assign blame. While adjusters often use the ",
          "marks": []
        },
        {
          "_type": "span",
          "_key": "s77q",
          "text": "damage location",
          "marks": [
            "strong"
          ]
        },
        {
          "_type": "span",
          "_key": "s77r",
          "text": " to conclude, their assessment is not final. It’s not unusual for an insurer to shift blame to limit liability, especially in borderline cases.",
          "marks": []
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "_type": "block",
      "_key": "b77u",
      "style": "normal",
      "markDefs": [],
      "children": [
        {
          "_type": "span",
          "_key": "s77t",
          "text": "That’s why it’s so important to have a legal advocate. Our team works to challenge unfair fault determinations by presenting more substantial evidence and, if necessary, litigating on your behalf.",
          "marks": []
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "_type": "block",
      "_key": "b77w",
      "style": "h2",
      "markDefs": [],
      "children": [
        {
          "_type": "span",
          "_key": "s77v",
          "text": "Steps to Take After an Accident to Protect Your Rights",
          "marks": [
            "strong"
          ]
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "_type": "block",
      "_key": "b77y",
      "style": "normal",
      "markDefs": [],
      "children": [
        {
          "_type": "span",
          "_key": "s77x",
          "text": "The first few moments after a crash can be chaotic, but they matter more than most people realize. What happens next can shape how your claim plays out—so here’s what we recommend you keep in mind:",
          "marks": []
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "_type": "block",
      "_key": "b781",
      "style": "normal",
      "markDefs": [],
      "children": [
        {
          "_type": "span",
          "_key": "s77z",
          "text": "Call 911 and get a police report.",
          "marks": [
            "strong"
          ]
        },
        {
          "_type": "span",
          "_key": "s780",
          "text": " This provides an official incident record and may support your version of events.",
          "marks": []
        }
      ],
      "listItem": "bullet",
      "level": 1
    },
    {
      "_type": "block",
      "_key": "b784",
      "style": "normal",
      "markDefs": [],
      "children": [
        {
          "_type": "span",
          "_key": "s782",
          "text": "Take thorough photos.",
          "marks": [
            "strong"
          ]
        },
        {
          "_type": "span",
          "_key": "s783",
          "text": " Snap images of vehicle damage, the road, signage, and weather—anything that paints a full picture.",
          "marks": []
        }
      ],
      "listItem": "bullet",
      "level": 1
    },
    {
      "_type": "block",
      "_key": "b787",
      "style": "normal",
      "markDefs": [],
      "children": [
        {
          "_type": "span",
          "_key": "s785",
          "text": "Speak to witnesses.",
          "marks": [
            "strong"
          ]
        },
        {
          "_type": "span",
          "_key": "s786",
          "text": " Collect names and contact details. Their statements may help prove what happened.",
          "marks": []
        }
      ],
      "listItem": "bullet",
      "level": 1
    },
    {
      "_type": "block",
      "_key": "b78a",
      "style": "normal",
      "markDefs": [],
      "children": [
        {
          "_type": "span",
          "_key": "s788",
          "text": "Get medical attention.",
          "marks": [
            "strong"
          ]
        },
        {
          "_type": "span",
          "_key": "s789",
          "text": " Even minor injuries can worsen. Documentation can now protect your health and your case.",
          "marks": []
        }
      ],
      "listItem": "bullet",
      "level": 1
    },
    {
      "_type": "block",
      "_key": "b78d",
      "style": "normal",
      "markDefs": [],
      "children": [
        {
          "_type": "span",
          "_key": "s78b",
          "text": "Contact a car accident lawyer. ",
          "marks": [
            "strong"
          ]
        },
        {
          "_type": "span",
          "_key": "s78c",
          "text": "Legal guidance early on can prevent mistakes and preserve key evidence.",
          "marks": []
        }
      ],
      "listItem": "bullet",
      "level": 1
    },
    {
      "_type": "block",
      "_key": "b78j",
      "style": "normal",
      "markDefs": [
        {
          "_key": "l78f",
          "_type": "link",
          "href": "https://dmv.colorado.gov/report-accident"
        }
      ],
      "children": [
        {
          "_type": "span",
          "_key": "s78e",
          "text": "According to the",
          "marks": []
        },
        {
          "_type": "span",
          "_key": "s78g",
          "text": " Colorado Department of Revenue",
          "marks": [
            "l78f"
          ]
        },
        {
          "_type": "span",
          "_key": "s78i",
          "text": ", any crash involving injury, death, or significant property damage must be reported.",
          "marks": []
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "_type": "block",
      "_key": "b78l",
      "style": "h2",
      "markDefs": [],
      "children": [
        {
          "_type": "span",
          "_key": "s78k",
          "text": "Scenarios of Fault Determination in Colorado",
          "marks": [
            "strong"
          ]
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "_type": "block",
      "_key": "b78n",
      "style": "normal",
      "markDefs": [],
      "children": [
        {
          "_type": "span",
          "_key": "s78m",
          "text": "Understanding how car accident fault by location of damage works is easier when you examine real-world scenarios. Below are a few examples we often encounter in Colorado:",
          "marks": []
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "_type": "block",
      "_key": "b78q",
      "style": "normal",
      "markDefs": [],
      "children": [
        {
          "_type": "span",
          "_key": "s78o",
          "text": "Rear-End Collisions:",
          "marks": [
            "strong"
          ]
        },
        {
          "_type": "span",
          "_key": "s78p",
          "text": " The trailing driver is usually presumed at fault, since they must maintain a safe following distance. However, a partial fault may be assigned if the front driver stopped abruptly without reason or had malfunctioning brake lights.",
          "marks": []
        }
      ],
      "listItem": "bullet",
      "level": 1
    },
    {
      "_type": "block",
      "_key": "b78t",
      "style": "normal",
      "markDefs": [],
      "children": [
        {
          "_type": "span",
          "_key": "s78r",
          "text": "Left-Turn Accidents:",
          "marks": [
            "strong"
          ]
        },
        {
          "_type": "span",
          "_key": "s78s",
          "text": " Drivers making a left turn are typically held responsible unless the oncoming driver ran a red light or was speeding. The side of impact can help clarify the direction and timing of the crash.",
          "marks": []
        }
      ],
      "listItem": "bullet",
      "level": 1
    },
    {
      "_type": "block",
      "_key": "b78w",
      "style": "normal",
      "markDefs": [],
      "children": [
        {
          "_type": "span",
          "_key": "s78u",
          "text": "Side-Swipe Accidents:",
          "marks": [
            "strong"
          ]
        },
        {
          "_type": "span",
          "_key": "s78v",
          "text": " Damage along both vehicles’ sides can suggest lane drift or unsafe merging. If the damage is near the rear of one vehicle and the front of the other, that could indicate an improper lane change.",
          "marks": []
        }
      ],
      "listItem": "bullet",
      "level": 1
    },
    {
      "_type": "block",
      "_key": "b78z",
      "style": "normal",
      "markDefs": [],
      "children": [
        {
          "_type": "span",
          "_key": "s78x",
          "text": "Intersection Collisions:",
          "marks": [
            "strong"
          ]
        },
        {
          "_type": "span",
          "_key": "s78y",
          "text": " T-bone accidents often result from one driver failing to yield or running a traffic signal. The point of impact helps determine which driver had the right of way.",
          "marks": []
        }
      ],
      "listItem": "bullet",
      "level": 1
    },
    {
      "_type": "block",
      "_key": "b791",
      "style": "h2",
      "markDefs": [],
      "children": [
        {
          "_type": "span",
          "_key": "s790",
          "text": "Potential Challenges in Fault Determination",
          "marks": [
            "strong"
          ]
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "_type": "block",
      "_key": "b793",
      "style": "normal",
      "markDefs": [],
      "children": [
        {
          "_type": "span",
          "_key": "s792",
          "text": "While damage location can offer important clues, it’s rarely the only factor. Here are some common obstacles that complicate fault determination:",
          "marks": []
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "_type": "block",
      "_key": "b796",
      "style": "normal",
      "markDefs": [],
      "children": [
        {
          "_type": "span",
          "_key": "s794",
          "text": "Contradictory statements",
          "marks": [
            "strong"
          ]
        },
        {
          "_type": "span",
          "_key": "s795",
          "text": " from drivers or witnesses.",
          "marks": []
        }
      ],
      "listItem": "bullet",
      "level": 1
    },
    {
      "_type": "block",
      "_key": "b799",
      "style": "normal",
      "markDefs": [],
      "children": [
        {
          "_type": "span",
          "_key": "s797",
          "text": "Missing or incomplete police reports",
          "marks": [
            "strong"
          ]
        },
        {
          "_type": "span",
          "_key": "s798",
          "text": ".",
          "marks": []
        }
      ],
      "listItem": "bullet",
      "level": 1
    },
    {
      "_type": "block",
      "_key": "b79c",
      "style": "normal",
      "markDefs": [],
      "children": [
        {
          "_type": "span",
          "_key": "s79a",
          "text": "Insufficient or unclear photographs",
          "marks": [
            "strong"
          ]
        },
        {
          "_type": "span",
          "_key": "s79b",
          "text": ".",
          "marks": []
        }
      ],
      "listItem": "bullet",
      "level": 1
    },
    {
      "_type": "block",
      "_key": "b79f",
      "style": "normal",
      "markDefs": [],
